-- title:
--   Splitting a p-divisible group by complementary bialgebra idempotents over a field
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field, $p$ a prime and $H$ a $p$-divisible group of height $h$ over $F$ in the sense of the project structure: a family of finite free commutative cocommutative $F$-Hopf algebras $H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ together with surjective bialgebra maps $H.\mathrm{transition}\,v : H.\mathrm{level}(v+1) \to H.\mathrm{level}\,v$ such that $\dim_F H.\mathrm{level}\,v = p^{vh}$ and the kernel of the $v$-th transition is the ideal of $H.\mathrm{level}(v+1)$ generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$. Let $\varepsilon_v, \varepsilon'_v$ be bialgebra endomorphisms of the levels with $\varepsilon_v\circ\varepsilon_v=\varepsilon_v$, $\varepsilon'_v\circ\varepsilon'_v=\varepsilon'_v$, $\varepsilon_v\circ\varepsilon'_v=\varepsilon'_v\circ\varepsilon_v$ equal to the unit composed after the counit, convolution product $\varepsilon_v * \varepsilon'_v = \mathrm{id}$ in the convolution monoid of algebra maps, and each family commuting with the transitions. The conclusion asserts integers $h_1+h_2=h$, $p$-divisible groups $H_1,H_2$ over $F$ of heights $h_1,h_2$, bialgebra maps $\pi_{i,v} : H.\mathrm{level}\,v \to H_i.\mathrm{level}\,v$, algebra maps $\sigma_{i,v}$ in the other direction, and bialgebra maps $\Theta_v : H.\mathrm{level}\,v \to H_1.\mathrm{level}\,v \otimes_F H_2.\mathrm{level}\,v$ such that each $\pi_{i,v}$ is surjective, $\pi_{i,v}\circ H.\mathrm{transition}\,v = H_i.\mathrm{transition}\,v\circ\pi_{i,v+1}$, $\pi_{i,v}\circ\sigma_{i,v}=\mathrm{id}$, $\sigma_{1,v}\circ\pi_{1,v}=\varepsilon_v$, $\sigma_{2,v}\circ\pi_{2,v}=\varepsilon'_v$, each $\Theta_v$ is bijective, and $\Theta_v = (\pi_{1,v}\otimes\pi_{2,v})\circ\Delta$.
--
--   This is the splitting of a $p$-divisible group over a field into a tensor (i.e. direct) product of two $p$-divisible groups of complementary heights determined by a pair of complementary idempotent bialgebra endomorphisms, the ranks being read off from dimensions over $F$ rather than from point counts, so that characteristic $p$ is allowed. It is used by [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_surjective_injective_ker_eq_map_of_comp_eq_self_of_field`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_surjective_injective_ker_eq_map_of_comp_eq_self_of_field), and rests on the Hopf-algebra results [`HopfAlgebra.exists_hopfAlgebra_surjective_injective_comp_eq_and_comul_mem_and_antipode_mem`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_hopfAlgebra_surjective_injective_comp_eq_and_comul_mem_and_antipode_mem) and [`HopfAlgebra.finrank_eq_finrank_quotient_map_ker_counit_mul_finrank_range`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.finrank_eq_finrank_quotient_map_ker_counit_mul_finrank_range).
